{"chunk_id": "857d139be378", "text": "Arjuna reaches a mysterious lake while searching for water and hears an unseen voice warning that he must answer questions before drinking. Ignoring the command, he drinks and falls dead instantly. Bhima follows, finds his brothers, but also drinks without answering the warning and likewise dies. When Yudhishthira arrives, he discovers all four brothers lying lifeless and mourns them deeply, reflecting on their strength and destiny. Suspecting a supernatural cause, he prepares to investigate. The Yaksha finally reveals itself and challenges Yudhishthira with a long series of philosophical questions about duty, knowledge, virtue, and human nature. Unlike his brothers, Yudhishthira responds calmly and wisely, demonstrating restraint, humility, and profound moral insight\u2014qualities that make this famous \u201cYaksha Prashna\u201d episode a central teaching moment in the Mahabharata about wisdom over impulsive strength.\nArjuna and Bhima die after ignoring a Yaksha\u2019s warning at a lake; Yudhishthira arrives, mourns, and begins answering the Yaksha\u2019s philosophical riddles.\nThemes: obedience vs arrogance, wisdom and dharma, death and testing, riddles and philosophy, brotherhood", "vector": [0.021886508911848068, -0.03282314911484718, -0.005408810917288065, -0.007769380230456591, -0.01327076181769371, 0.022719651460647583, -0.02332797646522522, -0.002674650400876999, -0.001585284131579101, -0.02517940290272236, 0.006079953163862228, -0.004198771435767412, 0.005471627227962017, -0.004876525606960058, 0.002319242572411895, -0.004942648112773895, 0.048851218074560165, -0.009336480870842934, 0.05961593985557556, -0.011716886423528194, -0.0017522431444376707, -0.001036468311212957, 0.014943658374249935, 0.01832912489771843, -0.006625462789088488, 0.027295319363474846, 0.009435663931071758, -0.02639605477452278, -0.005547667853534222, -0.00741893146187067, 0.00021427785395644605, -0.012338436208665371, -0.009071990847587585, 0.